Without the colour rule there are $3\times4\times3=36$ outfits. Remove those with two items of the same colour:
* two browns (brown jacket and brown trousers): $4$ shirts, so $4$;
* two blues (blue jacket, blue shirt): $3$ trousers, so $3$;
* two whites (white shirt, white trousers): $3$ jackets, so $3$;
* two yellows (yellow shirt, yellow trousers): $3$.

No outfit has two clashes (that would need all three items the same colour), so $36-13=23$ outfits are left.

**Answer: (A) 23**
